All other factor loadings such as Academic_Pressure, Family_History_of_Mental_Illness, Depression, Financial_Stress, Age, Gender, CGPA, Sleep_Duration, and Dietary_Habits were not statistically significant, as their p-values were all far above 0.05. In the structural model, Study_SatisfactionFactor did not significantly predict Sleep_DurationFactor (Estimate = 0.102, P = 0.968), demonstrating no meaningful relationship between these latent constructs. Covariances among latent variables were also non-significant (all P > 0.95).
